   "design": "Firms and agencies upload case files and program information to a secure client portal with a fixed request form, so the psychologist does not sort e-mail attachments. Advice uses a template that keeps medical details out of reports for employers. Once checked, the advice is released in the same portal. Meeting the parties and judging the case stay with the psychologist.",
   "previous_blocker": "Files came as e-mail attachments and advice was written from scratch.",
   "enabler_now": "Secure client portals with request forms are standard for practices.",
   "still_hard": "Employers want more detail than the client consents to.",
   "human_edge": "Advising an employer without breaking the client's trust.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "Nothing changes.",
